package at.bettertrack.web

/**
 * `app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/splash_bt_glyph.png`, base64 — the BT mark
 * the login screen draws above the wordmark, carried INSIDE the wasm binary
 * (web port, Phase W1).
 *
 * ## Why a literal and not a resource file
 *
 * It was a compose-resource first, and the resource is still in the bundle. It
 * does not work: `painterResource(Res.drawable.bt_glyph)` on CMP 1.10.3 /
 * Kotlin/Wasm fetches the PNG (the dev server logs the 200) and then hands back
 * a painter that draws nothing — proven by putting a `goldWash` background
 * behind the `Image`: the 64dp square painted, the mark did not. The FONT half
 * of the same library works on the same page, so this is the drawable path
 * specifically. Recorded in docs/KMP_PLAN.md §14 as R21, because W2 moves 2984
 * string keys onto this library and needs to know which half of it is load-
 * bearing.
 *
 * So the mark takes the shortest path with no unknowns in it: the exact same
 * bytes Android draws (864x864, 15,475 bytes, MD5 below), decoded once at first
 * composition. It costs 20,636 characters of source and ~15.5 KB of wasm — for
 * the one image the shell has, that is cheaper than a second asset pipeline,
 * and it is the strongest possible reading of "embedded, no external fetches".
 *
 * Regenerate with:
 *   base64 app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/splash_bt_glyph.png
 * and keep the two files byte-identical — the whole point is that the web and
 * Android cannot drift about what the brand mark looks like.
 *
 * MD5 of the source PNG: 55cbe77ccd8461b286a849e9c9c61b3a
 */
